# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is defence in depth for community decks: once Folio renders content it did
# not author, a sanitizer bug should not be the only thing standing between a stranger's markup and a
# reader's session token. app.js runs the sanitizer at ingest; this stops anything that slips past it
# from loading or executing.
#
# Only served over HTTP, so opening index.html from file:// is unaffected and the site still runs by
# double-clicking it.
#
# Why each directive is what it is:
#   script-src 'self'   index.html carries no inline <script>, and app.js uses neither eval nor
#                       new Function, so no 'unsafe-inline' or 'unsafe-eval' escape hatch is needed.
#                       Keep it that way — an inline handler anywhere would need this weakened.
#   style-src           app.js sets inline style attributes throughout (the globe's limb layers, drag
#                       positions, colour tags), which needs 'unsafe-inline'; styles.css @imports the
#                       font stylesheet from fonts.googleapis.com.
#   img-src             data: for the heightmap PNG data-URIs and profile avatars, blob: for the avatar
#                       upload preview, https: for card images hosted off-site.
#   media-src           https: for card and glossary videos linked from off-site (a <video src>). Videos are
#                       link-only — nothing is uploaded — so no data: or blob: is needed here.
#   frame-src           the two video hosts a link can be turned into a player for. youtube-nocookie.com is
#                       YouTube's own no-tracking-until-play domain. Nothing else may be framed, and the
#                       embed URL is always built by app.js from a matched video id, never from raw input.
#   connect-src         the Supabase project: auth, progress sync and the content_overrides overlay.
#   frame-ancestors     Folio is never meant to be embedded; this blocks clickjacking.
#
# If this ever breaks something on the live site, rename the header to
# Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only to keep the page working while violations still show in devtools.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' https:; frame-src https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com; connect-src 'self' https://qnrnjjcjeggzndgxtyqx.supabase.co; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
